{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggDKzWefbuf5wCP73Ymu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it, and `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`.\n\n**The cause:** `money.py` divided with `total // people` and threw away the remainder, so any amount that didn't divide evenly lost those grosze.\n\n**The fix:** it now uses `divmod` to get both the base share and the remainder, then gives the leftover grosze to the first people, one each. The shares always add up to the total and never differ by more than 1 grosz.\n\n**Tests:** I added two to `test_money.py` and ran them before the fix, when they failed. Now all 5 tests pass:\n- `split_cents(100, 3) == [34, 33, 33]`\n- A sweep of totals 0–249 and 1–7 people, checking that the shares add up to the total and differ by at most 1.\n\nThe person who pays the extra grosz is always first in the list. If you'd rather it be someone else, like whoever paid the bill, that's a small change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_read_input_tokens":19186,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"587d00e8-a450-4165-b175-528b2cd22b74","uuid":"3786ad74-1320-4e4d-89aa-c10634b92edb","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:14:47.479Z","request_id":"req_011CggDKzHWfkPHknSfzyNCU"}
